# LC bank 2 $D000-$DFFF (side A T04, loaded at boot). Here: its disk layer, $D000-$D653.
# A read-only RWTS in the ProDOS style (16-sector, 6-and-2, reads a data field in place), a track loader,
# and the section loader with its "wrong disk" prompts. The rest of the bank is game code (not yet read).
source ../mem/lc2.bin
include apple2.sym
sym SLOT16 $00
sym CKSUM $01
sym ADDR_CHK $02
sym ADDR_SECTOR $03
sym ADDR_TRACK $04
sym ADDR_VOLUME $05
sym BUF $06 2
sym TRIES $08
sym PAGE_LIST $09 2
sym TEMP $0B
sym TEMP2 $0C
sym TRACK $0D
sym CUR_PHASE $0E
sym ZP_SAVE $D400 32
sym PAGE_LIST_BUF $D470 16
sym PHYS_PAGES $D480 16
sym AUX_NIBS $D4AA 86
sym SIDE_MARK $6304
sym DISK_MARK $6303
sym GAME_SLOT16 $BFFF
# names from the leftover equates (side A T14 S8-SC)
sym DOTEXT $1A6A
sym WAIT $6225
sym ylow $19AA
sym yhigh $18EA
$0000 org $D000
$0000 code
$0000 label LOAD_SECTION_V
$0003 code
$0003 label TIME_V
$0003 note through JMPTIME ($1D2B): names from the leftover equates (side A T14 S8-SC)
$0006 code
$0006 label GOVER_V
$0006 note through JMPGOVER ($1D3B)
$0009 label DISK_SLOT16
$0009 db 1
$0009 note slot*16, from GAME_SLOT16 at the first LOAD_SECTION
$000A code
$000A label ERR_RTS
@$D00C code
@$D00C label READ_DATA
@$D00C comment X = slot*16, BUF = destination page: reads the data field after the address field just read.
@$D00C comment C = 1: no data field / bad checksum
@$D020 comment the destination is patched into the stores, $54 / $AC before it so Y can count $AA..$FF
@$D042 label FIND_DATA
@$D04C note D5 AA AD (a bad second or third nibble: compare it with D5 again)
@$D064 comment the 86 aux nibbles -> AUX_NIBS, then 3 passes of 86 merging them with the 256 into BUF
@$D0CD comment the checksum must be 0, then DE: CLC
@$D0D9 note to $D0DD, BIT's operand: CLC
@$D0DC note skips the CLC: C = 1 from $D0DB
@$D0E4 code
@$D0E4 label SEEK
@$D0E4 comment A = track: phases from CUR_PHASE to 2*A, 40 ms each (DELAY $28)
@$D100 label DENIB
@$D100 comment its code doubles as the denibble table's start: DENIB,X for nibble X ($96-$FF)
@$D10E code
@$D10E label PHASE_ON
@$D11A code
@$D11A label PHASE_WAIT
@$D11F code
@$D11F label ERR_RTS2
@$D121 code
@$D121 label READ_ADDRESS
@$D121 comment the next address field: D5 AA 96, volume / track / sector / checksum (4-and-4), DE AA. C = 1: none
@$D17D db $83
@$D17D note denibble table (indexed from DENIB) and the 6-and-2 merge table ($D200 + 4 * 2 bits)
@$D300 code
@$D300 label READ_TRACK
@$D300 comment TRACK, PAGE_LIST (16 pages by logical sector, 0: skip): reads them in any order, 255 address
@$D300 comment fields at most. C = 1: failed
@$D305 comment pages by physical sector, from the logical ones (PHYSICAL_TO_LOGICAL)
@$D318 label NEXT_FIELD
@$D31A note to $D34C, BIT's operand: SEC / RTS
@$D34B note skips the SEC
@$D34E label WRONG_TRACK
@$D34E comment seek again from the track the address field gave
@$D35B label PHYSICAL_TO_LOGICAL
@$D35B db 16
@$D36B code
@$D36B label READ_TRACK_AT
@$D36B comment A = first page: the 16 pages A.., then READ_TRACK. Failed: SIDE_MARK = $FF (wrong disk, ask)
@$D37A note the first page
@$D38C db $1A
@$D38C note unused: READ_TRACK_AT with the page list inline after the JSR
@$D3A6 code
@$D3A6 label LOAD_TRACK
@$D3A6 comment A = track - 1, Y = first page: one track, 16 pages, with the game's zero page swapped out
@$D3C6 code
@$D3C6 label SWAP_ZP
@$D3C6 comment $00-$1F <-> ZP_SAVE (the disk layer's own zero page, CUR_PHASE in $D40E)
@$D3D8 code
@$D3D8 label DELAY
@$D3E4 db $11E
@$D3E4 comment ZP_SAVE / PAGE_LIST_BUF / PHYS_PAGES / AUX_NIBS: work areas
@$D500 label SECTION_INDEX
@$D500 db 1
@$D501 label SECTION
@$D501 db 1
@$D502 code
@$D502 label LOAD_SECTION
@$D502 comment A = section: loads its tracks (TRACK_LISTS / PAGE_LISTS, by 8), then checks the $6300 page
@$D502 comment loaded: SIDE_MARK = SECTION_SIDE, DISK_MARK = SECTION_MARK, else asks and loads again.
@$D502 comment A = $FF: LOAD_TRACK X (track - 1) to pages Y.. (no check)
@$D518 label LOAD_SECTION_N
@$D522 label NEXT_TRACK
@$D546 label LOAD_ONE
@$D552 label SECTION_SIDE
@$D552 db 12
@$D552 note 0: side A, 1: side B
@$D55E label SECTION_MARK
@$D55E db 12
@$D56A code
@$D56A label ASK_FLIP
@$D56A comment wrong side: "PLEASE FLIP DISK AND PRESS A KEY." until a key or a button, then load again
@$D5A7 code
@$D5A7 label ASK_INSERT
@$D5A7 comment wrong disk: "PLEASE INSERT DISK AND PSESS A KEY" (sic)
@$D5E4 label MSG_FLIP
@$D5E4 db $23
@$D5E4 note game characters: A = $00 ... Z = $19, $27 space, $24 '.', $FF end
@$D607 label MSG_INSERT
@$D607 db $25
@$D62C code
@$D62C label FILL_MSG_ROWS
@$D62C comment A -> rows 0-6 of both hires pages (clears or sets the message band)
@$D62B label FILL_BYTE
@$D654 code
@$D654 label TIME
@$D654 comment the time screen? (JMPTIME), not read yet
@$DA6D code
@$DA6D label GOVER
@$DA6D comment the game over (JMPGOVER): A -> $80; A <> 0: LOAD_TRACK side B T22 to $B000 until $B802 = $9A
@$DA6D comment (asks to flip otherwise, $DFC5), JMP $B800
@$DF0B label TRACK_LISTS
@$DF0B db $60
@$DF0B comment section n: tracks - 1 at TRACK_LISTS + 8n, $FF ends; pages at PAGE_LISTS + 8n
@$DF6B label PAGE_LISTS
@$DF6B db $5A
@$DFC5 code
@$DFC5 comment code, over section 11's unused page list bytes
@$D34B operand $38
